     "Results prose says Z=2, whereas the Table 1 note explicitly says Cmcm Z=4 and the listed conventional-cell sites have multiplicities 4, 4, 4, and 8. Peritheos uses the conventional Cmcm cell and Z=4; Z=2 is consistent only with a primitive-cell count.",
     "Table 2 prints MgSiO3 a=2.250(3) A in row 3, inconsistent with b, c, and V=120.11(22) A^3; a near 2.450 A would be required. The printed 2.250 value is preserved, and EOS reproduction uses the independently printed volume."
